<title>USA: GTE files petition in U.S. Appeals Court.</title>
<headline>GTE files petition in U.S. Appeals Court.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>GTE Corp said on Friday it filed a petition for a U.S. Court of Appeals review relating to its earlier motion to halt the implementation of the FCC's interconnection rules.</p>
<p>The company said it would request a stay of the rules from the appeals court if the motion, filed last week with the Federal Communications Commission, is not granted.</p>
<p>The FCC rules outline the enforcement of the Telecommunications Act, enacted in February.</p>
</text>
